  "graph": {
    "id": "unified-example-item-triggered-memory",
    "name": "An item recalls a memory for its actual holder",
    "description": "Watch a real item mention, resolve its current holder, apply the supplied prompt to that actor’s authorized memory, and stage only that actor’s private proposal.\n\nSetup: Load Mara and Elias and replace both canonical avatar IDs everywhere. Create actor-private JSON mara-item-memories for character:mara.png and elias-item-memories for character:elias.png, each initially []. Edit initial-holders: this campaign currently gives moonstone-pendant to Elias; ownership is authored accepted state, not inferred from who mentions it. Edit aliases and mention.actorId for the actual speaking/viewpoint actor. This once-per-source example expects at most one matching mention; ambiguous lookup holds. Bind Prose and promptedMemory. Existing native memories are read per actor. The default recall-or-create explicitly permits a pending invented memory if none fits; choose recall with allowCreate false to require existing history. No native memory is silently overwritten. Apply adds the private proposal uniquely by canonical eventId; absence/no mention skips the memory call and file branch.\n\nInspect: On Send owns this generation. Generate Reply uses the ordinary SillyTavern connection. Auxiliary roles remain unassigned in this portable example. Review the final narrative and proposed consequences; Apply publishes a new swipe and settles staged writes. Preview and bounded runs never settle.\n\nGenerated suggestions are proposals. Quoted observations preserve source identity; notes never establish canonical events. Private records cannot be appended to public notes.",
    "schema": 3,
    "runtime": 2,
    "mode": "native-unified",
